  "question": {
    "text": "A metal wire of linear mass density of $9.8 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{m}$ is stretched with a tension of $10 \\mathrm{~kg}$-wt between two rigid supports 1 metre apart. The wire passes at its middle point between the poles of a permanent magnet, and it vibrates in resonance when carrying an alternating current of frequency $n$. The frequency $n$ of the alternating source is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eytT5",
      "text": "\n$50 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "h89KN",
      "text": "\n$100 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "d8AlN",
      "text": "\n$200 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6o4qS",
      "text": "\n$25 \\mathrm{~Hz}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$n=\\frac{1}{2 l} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{\\mu}} ; \\quad I=1 m$\n$\\mathrm{T}=10 \\mathrm{Kg}$ wt. $=10 \\times 10=100 \\mathrm{~N}$\n$\\mu=9.8 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{m}=9.8 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m} \\quad \\mathrm{n}=50 \\mathrm{hz}$",
    "image": null
  },
